  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 211 PM MDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nWith this synoptic setup, we will see much of the same weather \nover the forecast period. Friday starts us off with the ridge \nover our area. This will bring warm temperatures and dry air to \nthe CWA. The 700mb temperatures are in the mid teens to lower \n20C, supporting warm temperatures across the CWA, before \ntemperatures return to the mid teens on Tuesday, cooling the \narea down some. Fire weather will be a concern through this \nforecast period with dry air, gusty winds, and little to no \nchances of precipitation through Monday. Daytime RH values go \ndown to the single digits to teens each day with little \novernight recovery. Fire weather has the potential to become \ncritical with any increases in winds. Monday afternoon through \nTuesday, a trough starts building over the PNW, potentially \ndrawing in some moisture and giving some relief to fire weather \nconditions as it nears closer to our area.",
